Carry out followup f-cfs-code-hygiene on converged-forward-solve. The lead's direction (2026-10-12) is that dead code is deleted, not kept or ported, and tests that only exercise dead code are deleted with it. This node starts from main after the consolidation node polygon-moment-owner merged (its tip 775370a7c). Its work is already in the tree:
- the owner choice, clip_quadrature._straight_edge_monomial_moments, from a 600-polygon exact census;
- the separatrix_clip._traced_polygon_moments deletion;
- the delegation of polygon_monomial_moments, polygon_density_moments, _area_moments and padded_polynomial_current_moments to the owner (32d463cf7);
- tests/test_polygon_moment_owner.py.
Those names survive only because their callers sat outside that node's fence. This node removes them.

Done when:
(1) Duplicates deleted. Delete each surviving name and route every caller to the owner, using the centroid-shifted degree-two view where degree two suffices:
- polygon_moments.polygon_monomial_moments and polygon_density_moments; delete nova/equilibrium/polygon_moments.py entirely if nothing live remains in it;
- separatrix_clip._area_moments and padded_polynomial_current_moments;
- stencil_mesh._polygon_monomial_integral.
A name with a live production caller inside nova/ is kept only as the owner call itself, with no reduction of its own; say which and why in the fragment. Callers today:
- tests/test_polygon_moments.py, test_equilibrium_separatrix_clip.py and test_domain_participation_continuity.py;
- benchmarks/exact_clip_closed_form_floor.py;
- scripts/prototypes/support/geometry.py;
- scripts/clip_independent_representation/score_candidates.py, which used _polygon_monomial_integral as an independent oracle; the census's exact rational reference is the stronger oracle, so use it if the script is live, or delete the script if it is dead;
- scripts/ring_attribution, density_moment_projection, in_cell_order_study, own_node_interior_score and density_forcing_ladder.
Afterwards, a search for each deleted name over nova/, tests/, benchmarks/ and scripts/ returns nothing outside prose reports.
(2) Dead dependents removed. Every test, benchmark or script that only exercised deleted code is deleted rather than ported. One that measures something still live is rerouted to the owner. The fragment lists each deleted file with why it was dead, and each rerouted file. Prose reports (*.md) are historical records and stay unchanged. tests/test_polygon_moment_owner.py keeps its behavioural owner-accuracy tests; its source-text delegation checks are deleted once the names they guard are gone.
(3) The six GPU goldens under scripts/prototypes/ladder/compatibility that nothing reads are deleted. These are the .npz files without the -cpu suffix.
(4) The _double_precision test helper is defined once, as a fixture or helper in the shared test configuration, and the copies are removed. The copies are in tests/test_census_polish_compaction.py, test_census_spline_value_authority.py, test_forward_census.py, test_hex_flood_coil_nulls.py, test_limited_boundary_touches_wall.py, test_mask_threshold_consistency.py, test_oracle_axis_admission.py, test_shared_spline_authority.py, test_solovev_certificate_builder.py, test_stationary_point_admission.py, test_structured_read_census_rows.py, test_thomson_forward_model.py, test_topology_domain_partition.py, test_topology_limiter_contact.py and test_topology_o_qualification.py.
(5) Every assertion on inspect.getsource text is resolved. They are in tests/imas/test_diiid_forward_gs_match.py, test_connectivity_boundary.py, test_connectivity_trip_sufficiency.py, test_default_wiring.py, test_flux_surface_connectivity.py, test_forward_operator_domain.py, test_route_solve_requests.py, test_sol_support_selection.py, test_split_spline.py, test_topology_domain_partition.py, test_xpoint_cell_wedge_clip.py and test_polygon_moment_owner.py. Each is replaced by a behavioural test of the same guarantee, or deleted where the structure it guarded no longer exists. The fragment says which, case by case.
(6) The suites covering every touched module pass by delta against the base, on CPU in place. Use the H200 lane only for modules whose CPU compiles exceed the hour. The two stencil_mesh failures that fail identically at base are pre-existing; report them, do not fix them here. Report the net line delta; it must be negative.
(7) No new public surface.
(8) The current.book certificate rows at about 550, 2,000 and 5,000 cells (limited and diverted; harness scripts/prototypes/support/book.py) equal the rows recorded at merge 06cc5abe1 within 1e-13 relative, for both booked moments and image errors. Also, tests/test_read_ten_thousand_cells.py at 550, 2,000 and 5,000 cells still matches its committed goldens. Run both in one H200 job against this node's head. Read the base rows from the current.book evidence receipts.
(9) Write the evidence fragment docs/evidence/fragments/converged-forward-solve/code-hygiene.html with plan-evidence-for converged-forward-solve; reckon audit-doc must report 0 errors.

Do not edit:
- nova/biot/polygonanalytic.py or tests/biot/test_moment_path_parity.py;
- scripts/analytic_oracle_fixtures or tests/test_certificate_exterior_support.py, which the exterior node owns;
- scripts/prototypes/read_route, which the read-route node owns;
- nova/equilibrium/forward_operator.py, gs.py, forward.py or current.py, which the held wiring node owns.
If a deletion reaches one of these, stop and name it instead of editing.

Run conditions: H200 rows run as one job through RECKON_ALLOW_NESTED_LAUNCH=1 scripts/h200_test_lane/run.sh --log (an absolute path in the run directory) --wait -- (targets), or one sbatch job on --partition=betelgeuse --reservation=gpu_0003_grpA --gres=gpu:1 with rungs as rows inside the allocation (never an array), --time sized to finish, XLA_PYTHON_CLIENT_PREALLOCATE=false and TMPDIR=/tmp in the submit environment and in every child; submit for real and read squeue a minute later rather than trusting sbatch --test-only. On a compute node run /home/ITER/mcintos/Code/nova/.venv/bin/python directly with PYTHONPATH set to the run worktree and never invoke uv; every login-node uv command carries --no-sync and nothing runs uv sync. configure_dtypes() before any array and jax_enable_x64 asserted True. Gates pass by delta against orientation_base_sha in per-module fresh processes, both arms running the same test files with the repository root conftest, baseline_suite and after_suite as single-line JSON whose log_path names one log file and whose command is literally runnable. Any wait is declared on the job that finishes last as wait_probe ["sacct","-n","-X","-P","-j","(job id)","-o","State"] and wait_terminal ["COMPLETED","FAILED","CANCELLED","TIMEOUT","OUT_OF_MEMORY","NODE_FAIL"] as JSON lists, and names every job it depends on in wait_condition. The certified 550, 2,000 and 5,000-cell machines and exteriors are cached under /home/ITER/mcintos/.config/reckon/crew/runs/r-20261009T181553786165-proto-support/ordered/rows/cache and may be read in place, never written. Run filepath relativize over any evidence fragment before committing. Commit with conventional subjects and bodies at every step and write the manifest and commit before every job wait; the manifest commits line lists every commit; status is complete, blocked or failed, which the worker sets itself. No plan labels in source names or comments.

Import provenance: run each arm with its own tree as the working directory, and print nova.__file__ in each log header. python -m pytest puts the working directory ahead of PYTHONPATH, and the shared environment's editable install points at the main checkout. So an arm run from anywhere else measures the main checkout, which is how the consolidation node's first arms went wrong. If SLURM_JOB_ID is set you are already on the fleet compute allocation: run CPU gates there in place, at no more than 8 concurrent processes, rather than submitting to a debug partition.

